    ("G238", gate_static_function_checks),                                # v10.352 — Static AST function checks (smoke test enhancement). Catches two bug classes the module-load smoke test cannot: (1) undefined ALL_CAPS constants used inside function bodies — the v10.350 STREAMLIT_AVAILABLE pattern, latent NameError that fires only when the code path runs; (2) shadowing local imports that re-bind a module-top name AND have a use-before-bind in the function — the v10.351 get_stock_snapshot pattern, UnboundLocalError. Conservative heuristics: ALL_CAPS only for class 1 (canonical constant convention); use-before-EARLIEST-binding for class 2 (subsequent redundant imports tolerated). Class scope tracked for default-arg expressions. Wildcard imports disable both checks for the affected file. Scans 549 files (425 utils + 123 numbered pages). Found 1 latent bug during initial run (DATA_DIR typo in actuals_engine.py _add_initiative_kpis — fixed in v10.352). Audit cost: ~0.4s. Replaces a multi-batch dynamic-execution undertaking with deterministic static analysis.
    ("G239", gate_dynamic_render_smoke),                                  # v10.353 — Dynamic render-function smoke. Actually CALLS each render function in the dynamic_smoke RENDER_REGISTRY with a synthetic actor ('md001') and reports per-render status. Effective pass rate excludes intentional st.stop() access gating (1 case — render_sbu_performance) and documented skips (1 case — render_platform_health spawns subprocess.run for live diagnostics, by design). Catches runtime errors that G231 module-load smoke and G238 static AST checks cannot: KeyError on missing data fields, TypeError on operations, AttributeError on dynamic attribute access, state-dependent errors. Streamlit mock extended with widget defaults (selectbox/radio/etc return first option from list) and dynamic-mode session state (synthetic manager proxies so renders don't crash on `um.users.items()` patterns). The mock has two modes — `install()` for module-load smoke (keeps managers None so pages short-circuit), `install(dynamic=True)` for dynamic smoke (manager proxies iterate empty so renders complete). The dynamic mock is applied IN PLACE to the existing streamlit module to avoid re-import issues. 14/14 effective renders pass at v10.353. Fixed render_propositions_performance to use defensive next() with fallback (avoid StopIteration when selection doesn't match any registered proposition).
    ("G240", gate_cbs_baseline),                                          # v10.354 — CBS baseline snapshot foundation (first sub-batch of CBS-wired actuals arc). Locks the YoY reference: data/cbs_baseline.json (canonical current) + data/cbs_baseline_<YYYY>_<MMM>_<DD>.json (dated archive, immutable once written). Generated by scripts/snapshot_cbs_baseline.py via utils.cbs_baseline.snapshot_baseline. The baseline captures bank-level CBS aggregates (always populated where deposits/loans/npl/customer/dormant JSONs exist) AND per-RM + per-branch breakdowns (populated when accounts.csv is present; empty {} otherwise — sandbox-friendly). Once snapshotted at year-end close, the baseline is frozen — subsequent CBS refreshes compare against it for YoY growth deltas. Pattern Q: validate-before-save refuses to write a baseline that doesn't conform to cbs_baseline.schema.json. Items 3 (auto-refresh actuals on CBS change) and 4 (PBT computed from CBS transactions) build on this foundation in v10.355+.
    ("G241", gate_live_actuals),                                          # v10.355 — Live actuals engine + YoY sidecar (item 3 of CBS-wired actuals arc). Wires v10.354's frozen baseline into the actuals pipeline by computing YoY deltas after each CBS-driven actuals refresh and writing data/actuals_yoy.json as a sidecar JSON. Sidecar entries are keyed by '<staff_code>__<kpi_name>' and contain (current_value, baseline_value, growth_pct, direction). KPI → baseline metric mapping uses default patterns (deposits / loans / NPL / customer-count / loan-to-deposit) at the bank-aggregate and segment level; overridable via data/kpi_baseline_mapping.json. utils.live_actuals exposes refresh_yoy() (orchestrator), load_yoy_sidecar / get_yoy_for (BSC consumers), format_yoy_label (display helper). Hooks into actuals_engine.compute_actuals_from_cbs so the sidecar regenerates whenever the actuals xlsx is rebuilt. Falls back gracefully when baseline is absent (mapped_count=0, baseline_date='n/a'). Pattern Q validate-before-save enforced. Minimal BSC touchpoint added in pages/1_perform.py: collapsed st.expander after the header cards showing top growth KPIs for the selected staff member (best-effort, never breaks the main BSC render).
    ("G242", gate_master_prompt_sync),                                    # v10.356 — Master prompt sync (anti-drift lockstep). The master prompt is the constitutional layer; every batch MUST sync it. Locks docs/Master_Prompt_v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>.md to reference the current batch within a 5-batch tolerance window (allows in-flight work). Detects the 240-version drift that accumulated between v3.9 (covering v10.115) and v4.0 (covering v10.355). Sanity-checks the constitution hasn't been clipped — Charter §1 "One Question" present verbatim, all 11 mandatory standards present by heading. v4.0 is the recovery sync; v4.1+ batches must hold the lockstep. Pairs with the v10.356 cycle-break correction in actuals_engine (G128 was failing prior to this batch).
    ("G243", gate_virtual_bank_readiness),                                # v10.357 — Virtual bank readiness audit. Reconnaissance gate. Probes 8 simulator modules (virtual_bank, virtual_bank_core, virtual_bank_simulator, scenario_simulator, stress_testing, strategy_simulator, hybrid_scheduling_simulator, liquidity_stress) for clean load + self-test. Boots a VirtualBankCore + VirtualBankSimulatorEngine and executes a 5-day simulation (with v10.358 seeding, generates ~2,600 txns; pre-v10.358 generated 0 against empty bank). Runs 4 sample scenarios via ScenarioRunner with the test engine bundle. Surfaces virtual_bank.coverage_report numbers: active staff, KPI mapping coverage, BSC coverage %, KPI library dangling refs + unused, department-level BSC submission path. Captures Football Team Test chain status: 7 links from teller action to MD ROE tile, each marked WIRED / PARTIAL / MISSING. At v10.358: 5/7 WIRED (CBS→actuals, actuals→YoY, YoY→BSC, BSC→branch, branch→regional), 2/7 PARTIAL (teller→CBS bridge not yet built; regional→MD tile lacks bank-targets binding per roadmap item 2). Saves readiness report as data/virtual_bank_readiness.json with schema lock. The gate locks the baseline: load + self-tests + boot + scenario sample must stay green. Chain link improvements (PARTIAL → WIRED) are tracked but not enforced — future batches close them.
    ("G244", gate_seed_determinism),                                      # v10.358 — Virtual bank seed determinism. Locks the seed-the-bank helper (utils.virtual_bank_seed) reproducibility contract: same SeedConfig → same totals (deposits, loans, accounts). A regression breaks the deterministic baseline that v10.361's end-to-end Football Team Test integration test will assert against. Also locks ECOBANK_BRANCHES sync with utils.core.BRANCH_REGION (21 branches). Sanity-checks: small config produces ≥50 customers and nonzero deposits. v10.358 closes the v10.357 readiness audit's "empty bank" note — the boot probe now generates ~2,600 transactions against a seeded bank (100 customers, 200 accounts, 30 loans, 21 branches, 30 RMs pulled from data/users.json). Cost: ~0.1s isolated.
    ("G245", gate_cbs_writer_integrity),                                  # v10.359 — CBS persistence bridge integrity. Closes Link 1 of the Football Team Test chain (teller → CBS). utils.virtual_bank_cbs_writer.persist_bank_to_cbs writes accounts.csv + 5 aggregate JSONs (deposits/loans/npl/customer/dormant) to cbs_data/ in shapes actuals_engine.aggregate_cbs_by_rm + aggregate_cbs_by_branch + compute_bank_aggregates consume. Atomic (tmp+replace), idempotent (same bank → same totals), coherent (aggregate JSONs match accounts.csv totals — no drift between formats). G245 locks: self_test passes (covers atomicity + idempotency), end-to-end probe shows deposits_aggregate.json total matches sum of CASA+TERM balances in accounts.csv, accounts.csv has ≥100 rows for a small seeded bank. After v10.359 the readiness audit reports Link 1 as WIRED — Football Team Test chain: 6/7 WIRED, 1/7 PARTIAL (only Link 7 MD tile remains, v10.360's job). Cost: ~0.1s isolated.
    ("G246", gate_branch_single_source),                                  # v10.360 — Branch single source of truth (v10.361 strengthened). Locks data/org_config.json::branches[] as THE source for the bank's branch list. utils.core.BRANCH_REGION and utils.virtual_bank_seed.ECOBANK_BRANCHES are dynamically derived; FLEXCUBE adapter takes precedence in live mode. v10.361 deleted all hardcoded fallback dicts (_BRANCH_REGION_FALLBACK in utils/core.py, _FALLBACK_BRANCHES in utils/virtual_bank_seed.py) per Rule N1: no hardcoded tenant data, even as fallback. Missing org_config now returns empty dict (configuration error surfaces in admin UI) rather than masking with stale data. Cost: ~0.05s isolated.
    ("G247", gate_admin_crud_coverage),                                   # v10.361 — Admin module CRUD coverage. Locks that pages/7_admin.py + pages/_admin_org.py provide full CRUD for branches (Add + Edit + soft-delete via active=False) and staff (Add + Edit + Delete with protection check + audit log). Per Rule N1: configurable data must be manageable via the admin module so the system stays bank-agnostic and ops teams can manage their estate without code changes. Verifies: render_branch_manager exists with Add + Edit/deactivate; UserManager has add_user/delete_user/can_delete_user/save_users; create_user_form and edit_user_form are present in 7_admin.py; audit_log entries are written for BRANCH_ADDED and BRANCH_EDITED mutations. Cost: ~0.05s isolated.
    ("G248", gate_md_tile_binding),                                       # v10.362 — Link 7 of the Football Team Test chain (regional→MD tile bank-targets binding). Locks the wiring across bank_targets.json + CascadeManager._load_bank + pages/1_perform.py _is_md_view branch + actuals_engine._get_bank_aggregate_roles + compute_bank_aggregates. Also locks the v10.359 bridge category-case fix (LOAN→Loan, FIXED_DEPOSIT→Term Deposit) that v10.362 surfaced via end-to-end verification: pre-v10.362 the uppercase categories from the bridge didn't match actuals_engine's Title-case expectations, so bank loan aggregates were always 0. End-to-end probe verifies seeded bank → bridge → compute_bank_aggregates produces nonzero Loan Book Growth and Deposit Growth. After v10.362 the Football Team Test chain is 7/7 WIRED (was 6/7). End-to-end integration test = v10.363 → Charter §2 passes. Cost: ~0.5s isolated (runs seed + persist + agg).
    ("G249", gate_charter_section_2),                                     # v10.363 — Charter §2 Football Team Test end-to-end verification. THE acceptance criterion gate. Verifies: utils/teller_actions.py module present with fire_teller_deposit / fire_teller_withdrawal / find_first_deposit_account / TellerActionResult; canonical test file tests/integration/test_v10363_charter_section_2.py present; teller_actions.self_test() passes (9 internal tests); end-to-end propagation probe (seed bank → fire KES 100M teller deposit → persist via v10.359 bridge → compute_bank_aggregates) produces delta == fired amount exactly (no rounding drift, no missing transactions); latency budget of 5s respected (Charter §2 'real-time' requirement). When G249 passes, the chain is provably wired end-to-end and Charter §2 PASSES. After v10.363 the Football Team Test goes from "chain mechanically wired" (v10.362) to "end-to-end verified with assertion harness" — the acceptance criterion for the platform's executive viability is met. Cost: ~0.5s isolated.
    ("G250", gate_pbt_computation),                                       # v10.364 — PBT computation from CBS. Closes the highest-priority MD BSC gap: bank_targets.json has PBT|2026 = 650B but pre-v10.364 there was no proper CBS-computable actual (the placeholder was bank[int] + bank[fee] - bank[loans] * 0.02, missing OpEx and impairment). v10.364 wires utils.pbt_computation.compute_pbt_from_cbs into compute_bank_aggregates. PBT = Operating Income (NII + Non-Interest Income) - Total OpEx - Impairment, where: NII = Interest Income - (Deposits × cost_of_funds_pct); Non-Interest Income = Fee Income × (1 + non_interest_other_pct); OpEx from data/opex_data.json (configurable via admin/finance, bank-wide breakdown of staff/IT/premises/other); Impairment = NPL Stage 3 × LGD%. All factors configurable in data/pbt_assumptions.json (cost_of_funds_pct=3%, lgd_pct=45% per Basel, non_interest_other_pct=15%) per Rule N1. compute_bank_aggregates now also returns NII and CIR (Cost-Income Ratio) alongside PBT for executive drill-down. The PBTComponents dataclass exposes the full P&L breakdown so executives can see why PBT is what it is. Cost: ~0.3s isolated (runs e2e probe).
    ("G251", gate_flexcube_live_wireup),                                  # v10.365 — FLEXCUBE live wire-up. Replaces v10.361 None-stubs in fetch_branches_from_flexcube + fetch_staff_from_flexcube with real REST call patterns + mock-mode fixtures. Three modes now genuinely distinct: synthetic (returns None, falls back to org_config), mock (reads data/flexcube_mock_branches.json + flexcube_mock_staff.json — exercises the live code path against local fixtures), live (real requests.get to FLEXCUBE via Apigee gateway with OAuth2 bearer auth). Mock mode is the key v10.365 contribution: it lets us prove the live code path is structurally sound without a real FLEXCUBE. When Apigee gateway access is provisioned and mode flips to 'live', the same code path executes against the real FLEXCUBE without caller-code changes. Gate verifies: _live_/_mock_ helpers present; fixtures exist and are valid JSON lists; live functions actually call requests.get (not stubs); synthetic mode returns None (preserves priority chain); mock mode reads fixtures correctly. Cost: ~0.1s isolated.
    ("G252", gate_accruals_synthesizer),                                  # v10.366 — CBS accruals synthesizer. Closes the "0 income" stub gap acknowledged in v10.364: pre-v10.366 the v10.359 bridge wrote interest_income_ytd=0 and fee_income_ytd=0 ("accruals computed downstream"), leaving v10.364 PBT NII=0 from synthetic data. v10.366 adds utils.accruals_synthesizer producing plausible accruals: loans accrue interest = outstanding × rate × elapsed/365; all account types accrue monthly maintenance fees (configurable per type in data/accruals_assumptions.json: savings 50 KES/month, current 200, loan 100, term deposit 0). Default loan rate 14%; LGD already in pbt_assumptions; this batch only adds accrual factors. Synthesizer is a PURE module — zero upward utils.* imports (v10.364 lesson: utility modules must not import their consumers, even in self_test bodies). Bridge calls synthesize_interest_income_ytd + synthesize_fee_income_ytd for every account row (both real and phantom-loan rows). Determinism preserved: same inputs → same outputs (G244 extends to accruals). Charter §2 still passes (G249): teller deposits go to current_balance, not accruals. v10.359 coherence still holds (G245): aggregate sums unchanged by accrual fields. Cost: ~0.2s isolated.
    ("G253", gate_profitability_reconciliation),                          # v10.367 — Profitability reconciliation diagnostic (INFORMATIONAL). Measures the gap between A2Z's two parallel profitability engines: Engine A (utils.pbt_computation, CBS-driven, bank-level only, used by MD's BSC) and Engine B (utils.sbu_pnl_rollup, customer-driven via cost_allocation_rules.json matrix, drills to segment/sector/RM/proposition, used by Finance hub). Pre-v10.367 they were unaware of each other and produced different bank PBTs (90%+ divergence on small seed). v10.367 ships utils.profitability_reconciliation with reconcile() that runs both engines side-by-side, normalizes time horizons (Engine B quarterly × 4 → annual), and reports ΔPBT / ΔRevenue / ΔOpEx with named reasons (customer basis differs, revenue source differs, OpEx allocation differs). Also ships docs/PROFITABILITY_ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md — the structural review with the unification plan (v10.368-v10.372). CRITICAL: gate is informational — passes whenever the diagnostic runs cleanly; the delta is reported in the summary as a metric but does NOT fail the gate. Will ratchet in v10.370+ to require status=='CONVERGED' or 'TOLERANCE'. Cost: ~1.5s isolated (runs full reconcile).
    ("G254", gate_sbu_reconciliation),                                    # v10.368 — SBU PBT reconciliation identity. First concrete unification step from the v10.367 architecture arc. Adds compute_pbt_by_sbu() to utils.pbt_computation returning Dict[str, PBTComponents] per SBU. Σ(SBU PBT) == Bank PBT within KES 100. Six SBU buckets: Retail Banking, Commercial Banking, Corporate Banking, Treasury, Digital/Agency (operational — opex only, no customer-attributable income), and Unallocated (absorbs the ~0.7B OpEx gap between opex_data::bank.total_opex 7.9B and Σ(by_sbu.opex) 7.2B). Mapping in data/segment_sbu_mapping.json (Rule N1 admin-editable; handles all three naming conventions: segment_config locked codes AFFLUENT/CORE_MIDDLE/MASS/MICRO/SMALL/MEDIUM/CORPORATE; VirtualBankCore SegmentType RETAIL/HNW/PRIVATE_BANKING/SME/CORPORATE; opex_data SBU names). Bridge now writes customers.csv (cif, segment, branch_code, rm_code) as the companion to accounts.csv — provides CBS-native customer→segment lookup. Cost: ~0.5s isolated.
    ("G255", gate_branch_reconciliation),                                 # v10.369 — Per-Branch PBT reconciliation identity. Second concrete unification step from the v10.367 architecture arc. Replaces the legacy aggregate_cbs_by_branch naive formula with a proper allocation engine. utils.branch_pbt_allocator.compute_pbt_by_branch returns Dict[str, PBTComponents] keyed by branch_code; Σ(Branch PBT) == Bank PBT within KES 100 (drift absorbed by largest-OpEx branch to ensure exact reconciliation). Four allocation rules: fte_weighted (default per Q3 v10.367 decision), revenue_weighted, equal, hybrid (50/50 FTE + revenue). FTE source chain: caller dict → data/branch_fte.json → accounts-per-branch proxy → equal split. All rules admin-configurable in data/branch_allocation_rules.json (Rule N1). On seeded bank: 64 branches in result, delta -2 KES (well within tolerance). Cost: ~0.3s isolated.
    ("G256", gate_customer_reconciliation),                               # v10.370 — Per-Customer PBT reconciliation identity (THE ATOMIC UNIT). Third concrete unification step. Establishes per-customer PBT as the foundational ground truth — all other rollups (Bank/SBU/Branch/Staff) become Σ over per-customer. utils.customer_pbt_allocator.compute_pbt_by_customer returns Dict[CIF, PBTComponents]; Σ(Customer PBT) == Bank PBT within KES 100; Σ(Customer OpEx) == Bank OpEx EXACTLY (drift absorbed by largest-revenue customer). Four allocation rules in data/customer_allocation_rules.json (Rule N1): revenue_weighted (default — standard activity-based costing), balance_weighted (deposits+loans footprint), equal, hybrid (50/50 revenue+balance). On seeded bank: 100 customers in result, delta 6 KES. Cost: ~0.5s isolated.
    ("G257", gate_staff_reconciliation),                                  # v10.370 — Per-Staff PBT reconciliation identity. compute_pbt_by_staff returns Dict[staff_code, PBTComponents] as Σ over customers tagged via customers.csv::rm_code. Σ(Staff PBT including Unassigned bucket) == Bank PBT within KES 100. Returns ALL tagged staff (BRM/SRO/RO portfolio owners + Tellers/CSOs service staff) — role-based filtering for sales attribution is a UI concern downstream (join staff_code → role from users.json). Bank acknowledged design: in production CBS rm_code may contain mixed roles; v10.370 is role-neutral; per-transaction staff separation comes later via cost_allocation_rules.json matrix mode. Cost: ~0.5s isolated.
    ("G258", gate_target_hierarchy),                                      # v10.371 — Multi-level bank_targets schema. Fourth concrete unification step. Extends bank_targets.json from flat 2-segment <metric>|<year> to hierarchical 4-segment <metric>|<level>|<entity>|<year> where level ∈ {bank,sbu,branch,staff,customer}. Backward compatible: legacy "PBT|2026" migrated in-memory to "PBT|bank|all|2026" alias; file format unchanged for admins still writing legacy keys. utils/bank_targets_schema.py (~470 LOC, 16 self-tests) provides parser/composer/migrate/get/set/sum/validate primitives. validate_target_hierarchy enforces Σ(child level targets) == bank target within 0.1% tolerance (configurable); sparse populations OK (only checks levels with data); honors _force_unbalanced_targets override flag for admin edge cases. Closes the top-down half of the reconciliation: actuals atomic since v10.370 (G256), targets atomic since v10.371. G253 still informational (full convergence requires v10.372 Engine B refactor). Cost: ~0.05s isolated.
    ("G259", gate_system_state_review),                                   # v10.373 — System State Review document. Strategic review batch (no engine changes). Maps the 123 pages + 439 utils + 208 data files surface and identifies: (a) which roles need live action interfaces beyond teller_actions.py to enable real virtual simulations of every staff role per Joshua's directive, (b) which parallel profitability engines still exist (customer_profitability.py, rm_profitability.py, product_profitability.py) and would benefit from the v10.368-v10.372 unification pattern, (c) other modules (risk, customer 360, treasury/ALM, compliance) where the same pattern applies, (d) recommended phasing (A surface UI / B close remaining parallel engines / C live actions for every role / D module-by-module unification / E executive UI). G259 locks the document's presence + key sections so it remains the strategic anchor for v10.374+. Cost: ~0.001s.
    ("G260", gate_role_taxonomy_alignment),                                # v10.374 — Role Taxonomy Alignment (Phase A first batch). Establishes the profitability axis: every role in users.json + hr.json (126 distinct) classifies to portfolio_owner / proposition_owner / structural_owner / service / support — orthogonal to the existing seniority axis (role_tiers 0-6). Joshua: "ensure the tree also aligns from the pipeline management... eliminate ambiguities". Extends data/org_hierarchy_config.json with profitability_axis subtree (41 explicit role mappings + tier_keyword_fallback). Ships utils/role_taxonomy.py (12 self-tests) with classify_role / get_profitability_tier / get_branch_scope / get_sbu / can_be_tagged / validate_role_coverage. Coverage: 100% (41 explicit + 85 keyword + 0 unclassified). Taggability invariant locked: only portfolio_owner + service tiers may appear in accounts.csv::relationship_manager_code; proposition / structural / support MUST NOT tag. SBU values align with segment_sbu_mapping.json. Body-system analogy: this is the profitability circulatory system. Cost: ~0.05s isolated.
    ("G261", gate_staff_pbt_page),                                         # v10.375 — Role-aware Staff PBT page (Phase A second batch). First UI surface of v10.370 atomic per-staff engine + v10.374 profitability axis. Ships pages/120_staff_pbt.py (~290 LOC) with three role-aware filters (tier / sbu / branch_scope), a top reconciliation strip making the G257 identity visible to users (Bank PBT / Σ Staff PBT / Δ KES), four tabs (Staff ranking / Tier distribution / SBU contribution / Unassigned bucket), and a footer documenting the full data lineage. Resolves the teller-vs-RM framing from v10.370: data engine is role-neutral (every tagged staff counts); UI surfaces who actually OWNS the PBT via the v10.374 tier filter. Body-system view: this is the first UI making the circulatory system visible. Cost: ~0.005s.
    ("G262", gate_pm_framework_bridge),                                    # v10.376 — Performance Management Framework Bridge (Phase A third batch). Joshua's course correction: the entire system's primary purpose is Performance Management (BSC + KPI Library + Target Cascade); the profitability arc is one essential thread within it, not the whole. Ships docs/PERFORMANCE_MANAGEMENT_FRAMEWORK_REVIEW_v10.376.md (~14KB, 9 Parts) deeply surveying the BSC ecosystem (109 active KPIs, 4 main pillars, 227 roles in role_kpis, 1,051 cascade entries, 8,167 actuals records per period, MD has 12 KPIs including PBT). Ships utils/canonical_pbt_bsc_view.py — read-only bridge with get_md_pbt_summary / get_md_cascade_allocations / format_md_pbt_card / MDPBTSummary. Joins canonical PBT (v10.370 G256/G257 + v10.372 G253 ENFORCING) with MD's cascaded PBT target (target_cascade.json::300001|PBT|2026, G258). Enriches 12 cascade allocations with v10.374 role taxonomy (profitability_tier). Enhances pages/100_md_cockpit.py BSC Summary tab with a Canonical PBT 4-metric panel + lineage expander + 12-allocation drill expander + drill links to v10.375 staff page. **Read-only by design** — write-bridge (canonical engines feeding bsc_engine.submit) is deferred to v10.377+ once consumer mapping is complete. Documents drift discovered in PM framework (KPI-ID mismatch in role_kpis vs kpi_library, pillar weight drift 40/25/25/10 array vs 68/14/6/12 field). Cost: ~1.5s isolated.
    ("G263", gate_universal_bsc_contract),                                 # v10.377 — Universal BSC Data Contract + Virtual Bank KPI Flow Unifier. Per Technical Governance Framework §5.1: every module must output {staff_code, kpi_id, value, period, source_module}; Joshua's directive: "have our virtual bank unify how all KPIs flow, test all modules and ensure every staff works and is measured." Establishes the nervous-system layer of the body-system framing. Ships utils/bsc_universal_contract.py (leaf module — zero upward imports; 10 self-tests) with UniversalBSCRecord / make_record / validate_universal_record / validate_batch / records_summary + period format validation + source_module convention check. Ships utils/virtual_bank_kpi_unifier.py (~340 LOC, 8 self-tests) with unify_bank_pbt / unify_sbu_pbt / unify_branch_pbt / unify_staff_pbt / unify_all_kpi_flow. End-to-end demonstration: seeded bank → all canonical engines → 98 universal records (1 bank + 6 SBUs + 63 branches + 28 staff), 0 contract violations, Σ-identity reconciliation passes at every dimension within KES 6 (well under KES 100 tolerance). Codifies the official Technical Governance Framework via docs/A2Z_GOVERNANCE_CONSTITUTION_INTERNAL_v10.377.md (8 Parts). Read-only — write-bridge (canonical engines feeding bsc_engine.submit) deferred to v10.379. Cost: ~1.5s isolated.
    ("G264", gate_customer_master_merge),                                  # v10.378 — Customer Master Merge (Phase B continues). Per Joshua's "merge into 1" approval at v10.374 wrap-up. Establishes the recognition/sensory layer of the body-system framing: the bank recognizes its customers across both transactional (CBS) and intelligence (marketing) universes via one canonical engine. Ships docs/CUSTOMER_MASTER_MERGE_v10.378.md (~7KB, 7 Parts) documenting merge strategy + conflict resolution rules + identity equation + storage policy (no new JSON per §4.3). Ships utils/customer_master_canonical.py (leaf module — 10 self-tests) with UnifiedCustomerRecord / compute_unified_customer_master / reconciliation_summary / get_customer + STATUS_CBS_ONLY/MARKETING_ONLY/BOTH + SRC_CBS/MARKETING/DERIVED. Merges CBS customers.csv (100 seed / 700K production) + customer_intelligence.json (3,000 individuals, 9-digit CIF) + customer_intelligence_business.json (206 businesses, CIF<digits> format). Strict CIF match (fuzzy matching by name/phone deferred to v10.4XX). Conflict resolution: CBS wins for full_name/segment/branch_code/rm_code (KYC-authoritative); marketing wins for clv/churn/nba/nps/propensity_scores/tags/digital_engagement (analytics). Field-level _field_lineage tracking. Identity equation |A∪B| = |A| + |B| - |A∩B| locked. End-to-end demonstration: seeded bank → 3,306 unified records (100 cbs_only + 3,206 marketing_only + 0 both — disjoint by design in seed). Read-only — no new JSON file per constitution §4.3 (canonical engine IS the source of truth). Cost: ~1.0s isolated.
    ("G265", gate_canonical_write_bridge),                                 # v10.379 — Canonical Write-Bridge (Phase B continues). Closes the constitutional data-flow loop (§5.3 Source → Staging → Transformation → Clean → BSC Integration → Reporting) — the last arrow was missing before v10.379. Canonical PBT records from the v10.377 unifier now flow into bsc_actuals_*.json via bsc_engine.submit() — the MD's BSC tab gets its actual from the canonical engine, not the legacy management_accounts source. Ships docs/CANONICAL_WRITE_BRIDGE_v10.379.md (~7KB, 7 Parts) documenting safety design (default dry_run=True), idem-hash collision filter, period translation, reconciliation gate, and remaining SBU-head collision (Commercial/Corporate/Treasury → single Chief — documented constraint). Ships utils/canonical_bsc_writer.py (~280 LOC, 10 self-tests) with WriteResult / write_canonical_pbt_to_bsc / preview_canonical_pbt_writes / _should_write filter / _record_to_submit_kwargs. SAFETY: dry_run defaults to True (AST-verified by G265 — protects live bsc_actuals from accidental writes). Filter skips fallback records (SBU absorbed → MD; branches without configured BMs → MD) to avoid idem-hash collisions and silent data loss. Reconciliation gate refuses to write when v10.377 Σ-identity broken (per §5.5). Idempotent via bsc_engine's _idempotency_hash. End-to-end sandbox-verified: 32 eligible records written, 0 errors, idempotent re-runs, MD PBT readback via get_actual() returns canonical -7.9B. Cost: ~1.5s isolated.
    ("G266", gate_kpi_alias_resolver),                                     # v10.380 — KPI Alias Resolver + Deep Review (Phase B continues). Per Joshua's directive: "do a deep review of the target cascade and kpi library for more understanding and appreciation also on how they are configured, what can be fixed." Ships docs/TARGET_CASCADE_KPI_LIBRARY_REVIEW_v10.380.md (~15KB, 10 Parts) — surveys cascade structure (1,051 entries, 51 cascading staff, 21 distinct KPIs, 1 corrupted deadline|* metadata key), KPI library (185 KPIs/109 active, 4+2 pillars, 227 roles in role_kpis, three ID conventions: numeric K-codes / Title Case / SCREAMING_SNAKE), surfaces 34 orphan KPI IDs in role_kpis (referenced but not defined). Ships utils/kpi_alias_resolver.py (leaf module — 10 self-tests) with KPI_ALIASES (19 Class A mappings: TOTAL_NFI → 'Total NFI', LOAN_GROWTH → 'Loan Book Growth', COMPLIANCE → COMPLIANCE_SCORE, AUDIT_SCORE → 'Audit Score', etc.), CLASS_B_ORPHANS (15 documented missing KPIs: DEP_GROWTH, NIM, ROE, NPS, CIR, FEES_COMM, DIGITAL_ACT, NEW_CUST, ACTIVE_ACCTS, PAR, TRANSACTIONS, 5 LEGAL_*), resolve_kpi_id / get_kpi_definition / list_class_b_orphans / is_class_b_orphan / clean_cascade_dict / scan_role_kpis_coverage. Read-only — does NOT modify kpi_library.json, target_cascade.json, or role_kpis. Opt-in: consumers that don't import work as before. After v10.380: ZERO unknown orphans across role_kpis (everything either resolves via alias or is documented Class B). MD's BSC submission readiness: 4/12 KPIs resolvable directly + via alias; 8 Class B still need new definitions (deferred to Joshua-input batch). Cost: ~0.2s isolated.
