    ("G287", gate_v10401_period_harmonization),                          # v10.401 — Period harmonization (TC38 resolved). Three core files had inconsistent period schemas: fixed_kpis.json quarterly only (2026-Q1, 2026-Q2), bank_targets.json annual (PBT|2026), target_cascade.json annual (300001|PBT|2026). Pre-v10.401 regenerator used `union of quarters` workaround when checking if a KPI was fixed for the year — meaning if a KPI was fixed in any quarter, it was treated as fixed for the whole year. v10.401 fix: built utils/period_harmonizer.py leaf module (~250 LOC, AST-verified, 5 self-tests) with explicit annual-period support — get_fixed_kpis_for_period prefers annual key, falls back to quarterly union; get_quarters_for_year returns {Q1: kpis, Q2: kpis, Q3: kpis, Q4: kpis}; promote_quarters_to_annual derives annual list from union; validate_period_consistency checks annual vs union for divergence; set_annual_fixed_kpis sets explicit annual override. Updated utils/cascade_regenerator._get_fixed_kpi_set to prefer annual key when present (backward-compatible). Seeded explicit annual `2025` + `2026` keys in fixed_kpis.json by promoting from quarters (2026-Q1 + 2026-Q2 were already consistent — same 16 KPIs each). Now production admin can: (a) maintain quarterly granularity (MD per Joshua A1 changes lock state per quarter), OR (b) set authoritative annual list directly (faster, simpler when quarters always agree). Engine state preserved: 0 cycles ✓, 0 cross-branch ✓, 0 multi-sender ✓, 0 rep_critical ✓. Cascade size unchanged at 25,488 entries (2026 union = 2026 annual). 16 fixed KPIs for 2026: CX Score, Audit Score, Staff Productivity, CASA Ratio, PAR, Account Dormancy, Channel Dormancy, K010, K014, K016, K121, K129, K132, K134, COMPLIANCE_SCORE, NPL_RATIO. Backup at data/_v10401_backups/fixed_kpis.json.before + target_cascade.json.before. Cost: ~0.5s isolated.
    ("G288", gate_v10402_kpi_naming_consolidation),                       # v10.402 — KPI naming consolidation (TC39 + deep review per Joshua). Deep review of all KPI names across kpi_library/bank_targets/fixed_kpis/target_cascade surfaced 4 alias pairs (not just NPL): NPL Ratio/NPL_RATIO, New Accounts/NEW_ACCOUNTS, Net Interest Margin/NET_INTEREST_MARGIN, Compliance Score/COMPLIANCE_SCORE. Critical bug surfaced: NPL_RATIO and COMPLIANCE_SCORE were in fixed_kpis (MD reserve) but the user-visible human forms ("NPL Ratio" and "Compliance Score") were being cascaded — meaning MD's intent to fix was not being honored at the display layer; user-visible Compliance Score was getting allocated to staff despite MD intent. Pattern observation: each pair has one human-readable form (spaces, title case) used in BSC display and kpi_library name field, and one uppercase machine form (underscores) added in v10.329/v10.341 normalization batches. Resolution: canonical = human-readable form (matches user mental model + BSC + kpi_library). Migration: (1) Extended KPI_ALIASES with 4 new mappings (NPL_RATIO/NEW_ACCOUNTS/NET_INTEREST_MARGIN/COMPLIANCE_SCORE → human forms) + redirected COMPLIANCE alias from "COMPLIANCE_SCORE" to "Compliance Score". (2) Made alias map win in resolve_kpi_id — canonical decision overrides duplicate library entry presence. (3) Archived 8 active uppercase entries from bank_targets.json (preserved in _v10402_archived_uppercase_aliases meta block with old values for audit; cascade no longer generates them). Old values were: NPL_RATIO 7.5/8.0, NEW_ACCOUNTS 450/500, NET_INTEREST_MARGIN 5.2/5.5, COMPLIANCE_SCORE 4.5 — note these values differed from human-form values (e.g. NPL 3.0%, NIM 7.5%, Compliance 95.0%) and were unit-scale inconsistent (Compliance 95% percent vs 4.5 Likert scale); deferred reconciliation to Joshua. (4) Replaced 12 uppercase KPI names in fixed_kpis.json across all 6 periods (2025, 2025-Q3, 2025-Q4, 2026, 2026-Q1, 2026-Q2) with human forms. (5