    ("G289", gate_v10403_cascade_cleanup),                                 # v10.403 — Cascade cleanup batch. Pure data cleanup per Joshua deep-review findings: (A1) Deleted 10 EXEC-* synthetic chiefs from users.json (exec_cro/cco/coo/cfo/cio/crso/ccmp/cia/chro/ccmo_001) — these were residual seed-data placeholders; real chiefs at 300002-300010 + 300178. (A4 + E-C5) Added Admin role + EXEC-* prefix to cascade_regenerator EXCLUDED_ROLES filter at _build_staff_index — Admin is Joshua's monitoring/login account, not a P&L responsibility center. (A5) Cleaned 13 test entries from canonical_change_log.json (test_user/deep_test session pollution). (D1) Retired stale test_v10397_total_unique_codes_increased (asserted 1449, actual 1448 post-v10.399). (B1-B4) Marked 4 KPI library duplicates with _v10403_alias_of field: NEW_ACCOUNTS→K006, K069→K024 (Digital Channel Adoption), K048→K028 (Collateral Review), NIM→NET_INTEREST_MARGIN; full dedup deferred to v10.409 (will migrate references first). Re-regenerated target_cascade.json from canonical: 24,192 → 24,024 entries (168 phantom entries removed via EXEC-* + Admin filter). MD's cascade now correctly shows 10 chief recipients (was 20: 10 real + 10 EXEC-* synthetic). Cascade allocations to EXEC-*/ADMIN001 = 0 (was 616). Engine state preserved: 0 cycles ✓, 0 cross-branch ✓, 0 multi-sender ✓, 0 rep_critical ✓. Backups at data/_v10403_backups/ (users.json + target_cascade.json + canonical_change_log.json + kpi_library.json before-snapshots). Cost: ~0.3s isolated.
